"""directo — agent-first CLI for a Directo ERP instance (login.directo.ee).

This tool is designed to be invoked by agents. Run `directo help` to load the
full usage contract on demand — do not rely on memorised knowledge of its
surface. It is identity-free: it knows nothing about any consuming project.
Connection (database, credentials, location) comes from config/env/flags.

Directo has no public API; this drives the same browser-session endpoints the
web UI uses. Auth is a three-step ceremony (see `directo help`); the resulting
session cookie is persisted in the capability's state home and auto-renewed on
expiry.

Credentials resolve in a 4-tier cascade (first non-empty wins):
  1. flags          --username / --password / --db / --koht
  2. project env    .env.local then .env, walking up from $CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR (else cwd)
  3. user config    $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/directo/credentials.env (default ~/.config/directo/)
  4. process env    DIRECTO_USERNAME / DIRECTO_PASSWORD / DIRECTO_DB / DIRECTO_KOHT / DIRECTO_COOKIE
Same DIRECTO_* keys at every tier; the project you're in wins, process env is the
fallback (so a deployed host's injected env governs when no config file is present).
Configuration resolves as named connections — a project's connections.json registry
plus `--connection <id>`; `directo help` documents them. Never pass the password on
the command line outside a throwaway shell.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import hashlib
import html as html_mod
import json
import os
import re
import sys
import time
from pathlib import Path

import click
import httpx

